<title>SWITZERLAND: Zurich Group 1996 net profit up 30.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Zurich Group 1996 net profit up 30.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>				    (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net			 1,138.2	  vs    874.1</p>
<p> Div (regd, Sfr)		 7.2		vs  6.0</p>
<p> Gross premiums		 31,858.5	  vs 26,435.7</p>
<p>Capital and surplus</p>
<p>  before profit approp	13,685.8	  vs 10,708.7</p>
<p>Pre-tax profit   - non-life		    1,441.4	   vs 1,264.3</p>
<p>  - life			  337.1	     vs 165.1</p>
<p>  - total			 1,778.5	   vs 1,429.4</p>
<p> Earnings per share (Sfr)   24.3		vs 19.2</p>
<p> Investments		    114,751.2	 vs 86,056.5</p>
<p> Net underwriting reserves  101,699.7	 vs 74,402.3</p>
<p> Workforce			40,981	    vs 36,522</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Swiss non-life and life insurance company is Zurich Group. Zurich said the consolidation of new companies, especially Kemper Group in the United States, accounted for about half of gross premium growth. Gross premiums rose 7.6 percent in local currencies and 20.5 percent in Swiss francs.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
